  "_doc": "Slot map, v3 of 2026-11-07 (08-verbeterplan-ronde-3): the D1 'Wake-up call' briefing, stripped. P1 = headline, four benchmarked KPIs, three findings (F1 margin, F2 middleman with the folio, F3 fading welcome), F4 where we are full. P2 = the package scatter (three layers: cloud, A/B/C, a transparent hover layer for the package tooltip) and the focus swap: one recommendation (package A), the alternative B and C as the answer to 'why not renovate?'. v3: a brand row on both pages (lockup, masthead line), button-slicer tiles in the house style, 11 pt as the smallest text (R4, 12 pt since v3.1), and the tooltip page tt-package. Single source of positions for the HTML comp and the PBIR generator (project/tools/opzet_report.py). Canvas 1920x1080, 8 px grid, margin 32, gutter 16 (brand kit goodnight-inn-hanger). 'cards' are furniture (radius 12, Sheet fill, Seam hairline) drawn as empty textbox visuals UNDER the content. 'visuals' are Power BI visuals. state: null = always visible; 'shortlist' / 'plan' = the two P2 panel states swapped by display-only bookmarks. v3.1 (plan 11, 2026-11-09): kit goodnight-inn-wakeup, night header; the brand row is the reversed 3.1 lockup and an eyebrow (vignettes and pay-off gone), 12 pt (16 px) floor, so a few notes are taller; 'tiles' are inner furniture (z_tile_*, P2 shortlist state only). Canvas and card shadows: opzet_report.py with brand_canvas_v3.py.",
